From: Firmware Security Follow-up <security@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bpf compare iterator pointer types

CVE: CVE-2026-90217
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/linus/83608e303b95d07afba1c15da0b5d9e513c2f15a]

State-pruning code remains in verifier.c in this 6.18 source; upstream split states.c is mapped to that exact implementation.

--- a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
@@ -19500,7 +19500,8 @@
 			 * infinite loop check triggering, see
 			 * iter_active_depths_differ()
 			 */
-			if (old_reg->iter.btf != cur_reg->iter.btf ||
+			if (old_reg->type != cur_reg->type ||
+			    old_reg->iter.btf != cur_reg->iter.btf ||
 			    old_reg->iter.btf_id != cur_reg->iter.btf_id ||
 			    old_reg->iter.state != cur_reg->iter.state ||
 			    /* ignore {old_reg,cur_reg}->iter.depth, see above */
